\subsection{Global regularity}
The genuine estimates follow from the a priori estimates by the standard approximation. 

\begin{thm}\label{genuine estimate}
  Let $n > 2$ and $\Om \subset \bbC ^{n}$ be a smooth bounded pseudoconvex domain 
 that possesses a family of transverse vector fields satisfying Property (${\widetilde P}_{n-1}^{\#}$). %or Property ($P _{n-1} ^{\#}$). 
  Then the $\bar{\partial}$-Neumann operator $N _{n - 1}$ is continuous on $W _{\(0, n - 1\)}  ^{k} \(\Om\)$ for any $k \geq 0$.
\end{thm} 

\begin{proof}
Since the exact regularity of $N_{q-1}$ is equivalent to the exact regularity of the Bergman projections $B _{q - 2}, B_{q - 1}, B _{q}$ \cite{BS1990} and $N _{n}$ %and $B_{n - 1} = {\rm I} - \bar{\partial} ^{*} N _{n} \bar{\partial}$ are 
is exact regularity, it suffices to show that %The proof now we are going to prove the regularity of 
$B _{n - 2}$ is exactly regular.
Since $C^\infty _{\(0, n - 1\)}  \(\overline{\Om}\)$ in dense in $W _{\(0, n - 1\)}  ^{k} \(\Om\)$, it suffices to show $\|B _{n - 2} f \|_k \lesssim \|f\|_k$ for any $f \in C^\infty _{\(0, n - 1\)}  \(\overline{\Om}\)$. 
By \autoref{KohnA}, $\Om$ can be exhausted by a sequence of bounded smooth strongly pseudoconvex domains $\Omega_\delta$. It follows from \autoref{TTT} that if $\Om$ possesses a family of transverse vector fields satisfying Property (${\widetilde P}_{n-1}^{\#}$), then $\Om_\delta$ also possesses a family of transverse vector fields satisfying Property (${\widetilde P}_{n-1}^{\#}$) for $\delta$ sufficiently close to 0. 
Since (\ref{tttt}) holds on $\Om_\delta$ with the uniform constant independent of $\delta$, then 
the theorem follows from the standard argument (cf. page 148-149 in \cite{S10}). 

\end{proof}

