\begin{thm}\label{priori estiamte2}
  Let $n > 2$ and $\Om \subset \bbC ^{n}$ be a smooth bounded pseudoconvex domain 
 that possesses a family of transverse vector fields satisfying Property (${\widetilde P}_{q}^{\#}$). %or Property ($P _{q} ^{\#}$) for $1 < q <n-1$. 
  Then the $\bar{\partial}$-Neumann operator $N _{q'}$ is continuous on $W _{\(0, q'\)}  ^{k} \(\Om\)$ for any $k \geq 0$ and any $q'\geq q$.
\end{thm} 

\begin{proof}
  By \autoref{increasing} and \autoref{TTT}, $\Om$ possesses a family of transverse vector fields satisfying Property (${\widetilde P}_{q'}^{\#}$) %or Property ($P _{q'} ^{\#}$) 
  for all $q' \geq q$.

