\subsection{Glucose Subsystem Analysis\label{sec:glucoseSA}}
The reception of the glucose molecules by a cell occurs in both states $S_0$ and $S_1$. We first derive the impulse response of the glucose subsystem for both states in Sections~\ref{sec:anaS0} and \ref{sec:anaS1}, respectively. Then, we derive the glucose concentration in the environment and that detected by the CGM through convolution of those two states in Sections~\ref{sec:anaglu} and \ref{sec:anaCGM}, respectively.
