%\red{Furthermore, as seen in Figure \ref{fig:compare2}, the heap size utilization is generally lower in DeepConvLSTM compared to PatchEchoClassifier, highlighting a weakness of PatchEchoClassifier. In PatchEchoClassifier, the number of ESN parameters significantly impacts heap size.}

From Figure \ref{fig:compare3}, when focusing on power consumption reduction, Patch
$\mbox{EchoClassifier}_{p=32}^{1000}$ and $\mbox{PatchEchoClassifier}_{p=64}^{1000}$ exhibit better performance than DeepConvLSTM with comparable energy consumption. However, for 
$\mbox{PatchEchoClassifier}_{p=128}^{1000}$, DeepConvLSTM outperforms in terms of accuracy. From this perspective, PatchEchoClassifier demonstrates superior performance compared to conventional CNN models while maintaining low power consumption.

Based on these comparisons, PatchEchoClassifier is not well-suited for IoT devices where memory efficiency is a priority. However, it appears to be a promising candidate for edge AI applications, where energy efficiency is crucial while maintaining high performance. Furthermore, comparing PatchMixerClassifier and PatchEchoClassifier, it was found that PatchEchoClassifier can reduce energy consumption more effectively.

\section{Discussion}
%\section{議論}
%本研究では, 当初, DeiTの原著論文でソフト蒸留よりも高い精度を達成したハード蒸留を実装することを目指していた. しかし, 一次元信号データを用いた実験では, ハード蒸留による損失の大幅な削減は見られず, 学習が期待通りに進行しなかった. 一方で, 本研究で採用したDeiTのソフト蒸留法では, 損失が一貫して減少し, スムーズな学習が可能となった. 

In this research, we initially intended to implement hard distillation, which achieved higher accuracy than soft distillation in the original DeiT paper. However, in our experiments with one-dimensional signal data, hard distillation did not result in significant loss reduction, and learning did not proceed as expected. In contrast, the soft distillation method from DeiT, which was employed in this study, allowed for consistent loss reduction and smooth training.\\

%また, エッジ用のLLMとして運用可能かどうか確かめるために行なった実験の結果, 推論の実行時間, モデルのfootprintサイズ, PatchEchoClassifierの推論における占有ヒープ領域の面においては, PatchMixerClassifierよりも優れていることが分かった. また, SHLの分類タスクのaccuracyにおいては, PatchMixerClassifierに劣るものの70\%程度が達成できており, モデルのサイズなどを考えると, 十分であると考えている.\\

%一方で, バックボーンとして必要なpythonライブラリの容量が大きすぎるため, エッジにおいて運用する際に問題になる点が課題である.\\

Additionally, in an experiment conducted to determine whether PatchEchoClassifier is suitable for edge deployment, it was found to outperform PatchMixerClassifier in terms of inference execution time, model footprint size, and heap memory usage during inference. Moreover, in the classification task of SHL 2023, although PatchEchoClassifier falls short of PatchMixerClassifier in terms of accuracy, it still achieves an accuracy in the 80\% range. Considering the model's energy consumption, this performance is deemed sufficient. On the other hand, the large size of the required Python libraries for the backbone poses a challenge for deployment on edge devices.\\


%また, 教師モデルとしてCNNベースのモデルを使用することも検討した. しかし, MLP-Mixerを用いた蒸留実験では, 生徒モデルが91.8の精度を達成した. MLP-Mixerを教師モデルとして使用した場合と精度に大きな差がなかったため, CNNベースのモデルは使用しないことに決定した.

%We also considered using a CNN-based model as the teacher model. However, during the distillation experiment with the MLP-Mixer, the student model achieved an accuracy of 91.8. Since there was no significant difference in accuracy compared to using MLP-Mixer as the teacher model, we decided not to use the CNN-based model.\\

%データ拡張に関しては, 信号版のCutMixを導入し, MLP-MixerからPatchEchoClassifierへの蒸留を行った. しかし, 精度は49.6に低下し, このアプローチはあまり効果的ではないことがわかった.

%In terms of data augmentation, we introduced the signal version of CutMix and performed distillation from the MLP-Mixer to PatchEchoClassifier. However, the accuracy dropped to 49.6, indicating that this approach was not very effective.\\

%MLP-Mixerの精度に対して10%以内の差でPatchEchoClassifierの性能を達成するため, アンサンブル学習の採用を検討しました. しかし, 単純にアンサンブル学習を適用しただけでは良好な結果は得られませんでした. 3つの並列な$\mbox{PatchEchoClassifier}^{4000}$モデルを用いたアンサンブルモデルでは, 精度は58.9であり, 単一の$\mbox{PatchEchoClassifier}^{8000}$モデルの精度よりも低い結果となりました.

To achieve PatchEchoClassifier performance within a 10\% accuracy difference from the MLP-Mixer, we considered employing ensemble learning. However, simply applying ensemble learning did not yield good results. In an ensemble model where three parallel $\mbox{PatchEchoClassifier}^{4000}$ models were used, the accuracy was 58.9\blue{\%}, which was lower than the accuracy of a single $\mbox{PatchEchoClassifier}^{8000}$ model.

\section{Conclusions and Further Avenues}\label{結論}
%\section{結論と今後の展望}
%本研究では, パッチ埋め込みとリザバーを組み合わせた新しい時系列モデルPatchEchoClassifierと, エネルギー効率を実現するためのカスタマイズされた蒸留主法の2つを提案した. 

%PatchEchoClassifierは, MLP-Mixerベースのモデルと比較して短い推論時間を示し, 60%を超える精度を達成した. これは, 人工知能における高い電力消費の課題に対処する可能性を示している. 

We proposed two models: a new time-series model PatchEchoClassifier that incorporates tokenizer and a reservoir, and a tailored distillation method to achieve energy efficiency. PatchEchoClassifier achieved over 80\% accuracy while maintaining lower energy consumption compared to MLP-Mixer-based models. Additionally, the comparison of energy consumption and performance demonstrated that PatchEchoClassifier achieves higher efficiency and superior performance compared to the existing CNN model, DeepConvLSTM, particularly in scenarios where power consumption needs to be minimized. This highlights its potential in addressing the current issue of high power consumption in artificial intelligence.\\


%今後の課題として, モデル構造や学習方法を改善し, MLP-Mixerに匹敵する精度を達成するリザバーネットワークを実現することを目指す. 蒸留法の改善として, トークンを損失関数に組み込む方法の修正を模索している. さらに, 量子化などの他の技術と組み合わせることで, よりエネルギー効率の高いモデルの開発を目指す.

For future work, we aim to improve the model structure and learning methods to achieve a reservoir network that reaches comparable accuracy to the MLP-Mixer. As for improving the distillation method, we are exploring modifications to how the tokens are incorporated into the loss function. Additionally, we seek to further reduce energy consumption and develop a model that outperforms existing methods. Furthermore, by combining other techniques, such as quantization, we aim to develop a more energy-efficient model.


