\subsubsection{Storyline and Game Rules}
Previous studies have shown that the use of themes and storylines can enhance users’ involvement and intentional engagement \cite{berson2018excursion, bouchard2019virtual}. The storyline for this game is shown in the Appendix \ref{sec:story}. In addition, clear game rules are essential to ensure that both players and agents can fully engage in the game. The rules of our game are outlined in Block \ref{gamerule}.

Our storyline is not designed to be result-oriented (such as emphasizing score incentives or win-and-lose), but to encourage users to fully express their true thoughts and behaviors. We minimized the focus on game mechanics to avoid interference with personality assessment \cite{jia2016personality}. Similarly, we applied this principle to the game UI by hiding scores and the number of game rounds.

