The functioning of the cognition module within the agent is illustrated in Fig. \ref{fig:fig6}. In this example, the agent begins by accessing its memory to review previous rounds of the game, including both the game and chat histories. It recalls specific instances where the player consistently chose to cooperate, which informs its next dialogue and decision. Next, the agent reflects on the extent of the player's cooperation, noting that the player values both cooperation and the competitive aspects of the game. At the same time, the agent is alerted to the player's tendency to defect in previous rounds. By considering memory, reflection, and ToM, the agent reasons through potential future scenarios, predicting the player’s next move. The yellow highlighted section fully demonstrates this and shows the importance of \textbf{CoT} and \textbf{ToM} in the system. Finally, the agent makes a plan for the next round based on the gathered information and reasoning process.

