\subsection{Implementation of Multi-type Perception}

The perception module acts as the agent’s sensory system. In our system, the agent perceives text/dialogue, behavior, and fine-grained personality traits and emotions (as shown in the blue block of Fig. \ref{fig:fig5}). The user's dialogue and game behavior provide the game context for the LLM agents, while fine-grained personality traits reflect traits demonstrated by the user during fragmented interactions, such as indecision in a specific dialogue round. Emotion data represents the emotional labels associated with each sentence made by the user. The prompts are provided in Appendix \ref{emotion} and \ref{Fine-grained}.


Fine-grained personality traits and emotion data, combined with basic dialogue and behavior information, support personality assessment. Additionally, the agent continuously learns from interactions, adapting its behavior accordingly. This multi-type perception module supports the agent’s decision-making and improves the system’s understanding of the user’s personality.

