By a standard linear algebra argument, it follows that
\[
\vt{X}(b)\in\mathrm{span}\left(\mathbf{1},\vt{u}(a)-\vt{u}(b),\vt{X}(a)\right).
\]
Noting that, for any vector $\vt{v}$, $\bar{\vt{v}}$ differs from $\vt{v}$ by a scalar multiple of $\vt{1}$, and that $\vt{v}\perp \vt{1}$, we obtain
\[
\bar{\vt{X}}(b)=\rho\left(\bar{\vt{u}}(a)-\bar{\vt{u}}(b)\right)+\sigma\bar{\vt{X}}(a)
