\begin{lem}
\label{lem:Splitting action}Suppose action $a$ splits the adjacency graph into $B_0$ and $B_1$. Then, for
any pair of beliefs $p_0$ and $p_1$ such that, for each $i$, some action $b_{i}\in B_{i}$
is optimal at $p_{i}$ in the decision problem, there is a convex combination $p=\alpha p_{1}+\left(1-\alpha\right)p_{0}$
such that $a$ is optimal at $p$.
