\section{Limitations}
\label{sec:limitation}

Our approach accelerates $\rm{SO}(3)$‑equivariant tensor products by replacing the full CG tensor product with a low‑rank CP decomposition. We substantiate both its theoretical speed‑up and its empirical efficacy across multiple benchmarks. A principal limitation is that the minimal rank required to achieve a desired approximation error is not known and determining it exactly is NP‑hard. To address this for the CG product, we introduce an empirical rank scheduler; however, this scheduler relies on the CG tensor and must be re‑derived for each new equivariant tensor product. In future work, we will investigate the general relationship between group‑equivariant tensor products and their optimal rank profiles, with the goal of developing broadly applicable rank‑selection strategies.

