\noindent A spanning tree of a connected planar graph $\mathcal{G}$, is a connected, acyclic sub-graph that includes all  vertices of $\mathcal{G}$. 
The determinant of a link $L$, denoted by $\det(L)$, is a well-known numerical invariant of links, which can be determined  by counting   the number of spanning trees in a checkerboard graph of a  link projection. Let us now  review this computation  method.
\begin{figure}[!ht] {\centering\includegraphics[scale=.8]{Fig/2.jpg}
