	\centering
    \vskip -0.3cm
	\includegraphics[width=0.45\textwidth]{FigPotentialsE}\hskip 1cm
    \includegraphics[width=0.45\textwidth]{FigPotentialsE2}
	\caption{ {\it Left panel:} The simple potential in Eq.~(\ref{simple model: V of phi}) (solid blue)
    and the more realistic one with $\eta_0>0$ (dashed red) and $\eta_0<0$ (dashed black), given in parametric form in Eqs.~(\ref{realistic model: phi of alpha})--(\ref{realistic model: V of alpha}). {\it Right panel:} Near the minimum both potentials exhibit a rather flat section, in which the USR period occurs. A zoomed-in image of the potential reveals a gentle slope around $\phi_0$ caused by $\eta_0\neq 0$. The potential can be continued past the asymptotic field value $\phi_0$, for example by gluing a constant $V=V_0$ part, or a symmetric image - see \eqref{potential around minimum}.}
