\subsubsection{Iterative Time Reversal} The iterative time reversal (ITTR) method \cite{stefanov2009thermoacoustic} uses TR on each iteration step, to refine
the current approximation to $p_{0}$. The next approximation $\tilde{p}_{0}^{(k+1)}(x)$
is defined through the previous approximation $\tilde{p}_{0}^{(k)}(x)$ by
the formula%
\begin{equation}
\tilde{p}_{0}^{(k+1)}=\tilde{p}_{0}^{(k)}+\mathcal{A}^\triangleleft \left( g-\mathcal{A}
\tilde{p}_{0}^{(k)}\right) ,\quad k=0,1,2,3,...
\label{E:iterative}
\end{equation}%
with $\tilde{p}_{0}^{(0)}=0$ and where $\mathcal{A}$ is the operator that solves (\ref{E:3Dwave}).


