where $B(x;\alpha, \beta) = \int_{0}^{b} t^{\alpha-1} (1-t)^{\beta-1} \,dt$ is the incomplete beta function, and $\tilde{\epsilon}=\frac{0.5+\epsilon_0}{1+\epsilon_0+\epsilon_1}$. 

Note that $u(W^X,\cutpoint)$ is bounded in $[0,1]$ under the condition of \eqref{eq:epbeta:constraint} by Lemma~\ref{thm:app:nonnegative:u}, which implies $\big| u\big(W^X, W^\categZorC,\cutpoint\big)\big|\leq \delta$.
