\section{Empirical Evaluations}

Our empirical evaluations focus on CIFAR-10, as the MNIST-like datasets (MNIST, FashionMNIST, etc.) have low discretization gaps (cf. \Cref{appendix: mnist like data performance}). CIFAR-10 and MNIST were also the datasets \citet{NEURIPS2022_0d3496dd, NEURIPS2024_db988b08} mostly focused on. %\footnote{Personal communications with Felix Petersen with experimental confirmation in \Cref{appendix: mnist like data performance}.} 
Due to constrained resources, we limit experiments by default to 48 GPU hours.
We use the hyperparameters from \citep{NEURIPS2022_0d3496dd, NEURIPS2024_db988b08} whenever possible rather than tuning the parameters, such as learning rate, ourselves. \Cref{appendix: hyperparameters} contains all the  default parameters. 

