As mentioned in the previous section, the noise component ($\Delta n=n_*-n_0$) almost surely does not satisfy the slope integrability condition (eq.~\ref{eq:commutability_constraint_nvect}). Therefore, when $n_*$ is disturbed from the $n$-vector of a surface, the most probable surface $\Gamma_*$ (eq.~\ref{eq:optimaloptimal_explicit}) for given $n_*$ could selectively remove the noise in $n_*$. 


