\subsection{A bowl shape}
\label{subsec:synthetic2}
The second test treats a bowl-shaped surface shown in Fig.~\ref{fig:synth3}, which is similar to the result of our actual data analysis concerning the 2013 Balochistan earthquake (\S\ref{eq:apptoEQ}). 
The elevation $z$ is expressed by a function that is parabolic along the long side $x$ and linear along the short side $y$ (see Fig.~\ref{fig:synth3} caption). When $x$ is interpreted as the horizontal axis and $y$ as the vertical, the surface horizontally bends well at the top and increases vertical tilts at the horizontal end (larger $|z_{,x}|$ for larger $y$ and larger $z_{,y}$ for larger $|x|$, roughly speaking).


