 The horizontal axis $1-n_*\cdot n_0$ represents the noise level of input $n$-vectors $n_*$ from the ground truth $n_0$. 
 The vertical axis $1-\hat n\cdot n$ in (a) and (b) represents the errors $1-\hat n\cdot n_0$ (red) and the residuals $1-\hat n\cdot n_*$ (blue) of $n$-vector estimates $\hat n$. 
 The vertical axis $|\hat z-z_0|$ in (c) and (d) represents the error of estimated elevation $\hat z$ from the ground truth $z_0$ (orange). 
