\subsection{Numerical simulations}

In this section, we would like to illustrate the behavior of System \eqref{eq:our_system} with numerical simulations performed in \textit{Wolfram Mathematica}. For this purpose, we will use fixed values of the model parameters (see Table \ref{table1}), selected initial conditions, and values of $N$. Moreover, we will need the explicit forms of the $G_T$ and $G_S$ functions. Under Assumption \ref{assumption:explicit_functions} we get


\begin{equation*}
    \begin{aligned}
    G_i(N)=&\,g_i\Big(\frac{1}{\mu_u}  f_u\Big(\frac{a_{y,C}N}{\mu_y \mu_C}\Big)\Big)\frac{N}{\mu_C}\\
